      "widgets_values": [
        "## ltx-t2v-portrait (lab)\n\nWhat this graph does: Vertical text→video (~10 s) tram-corridor track with a violinist.\nModels: LTX distilled FP8 UNET + DualCLIP (gemma_3_12B_it_fp4_mixed + ltx-2.3_text_projection_bf16, type ltxv) + LTX23 video/audio VAEs (joint AV empty audio latents required before KSampler).\nSampler: euler · simple · CFG 1.0 · 241 frames @ 24 fps ≈ 10.0 s · 512×768.\n\nPRIMARY OUTPUT — MP4 (easy to watch)\n• Node: Save video (MP4) = VHS_VideoCombine (format video/h264-mp4, 24 fps).\n• After Queue: open that node for an inline video preview.\n• File also under ComfyUI/output/ as ez_ltx_t2v_portrait_video_*.mp4 (comfy-state volume).\n• Frames still saved via SaveImage prefix ez_ltx_t2v_portrait for inspection.\n\nPrompting (LTX-2.3 + Gemma DualCLIP):\n• Describe actions over time (camera path + subject/environment motion).\n• For longer clips, write a beginning → middle → end timeline.\n• Negatives target temporal artifacts (morphing, flicker, jitter) if you raise CFG.\n\nHow to run:\n1. Review prompts / LoadImage; Queue.\n2. Watch Save video (MP4) preview; optional: open output/*.mp4.\n\nStack installs ComfyUI-VideoHelperSuite (VHS) + system/imageio ffmpeg.\nJoint AV: LTXVEmptyLatentAudio + concat required; audio latent unused (not saved).\nOptional offline: stitch PNG frames with host ffmpeg if you only need frames."
      ],
      "title": "Operator note — video output"
    },
